From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 19:30:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 08/25] isolate: add queue delay control and deployment lane

Add opt-in bounded independent-action, ordinary, dependency, and control-plane
queue lanes while preserving improved upstream CoDel as the default. Select the
oldest eligible external request, keep deadline-driven expiry active while no
worker class is eligible, and exempt dependency and control-plane work from
inappropriate adaptive shedding.

Retain each external entry's hard deadline through low-priority active-
JavaScript permit acquisition before worker assignment. Keep a non-consuming
expiry companion polled while a selected request waits for that permit, so every
other retained entry still expires at its own deadline. Give the companion
independent wake and timer state without making it a consuming receiver or
keeping admission open after scheduler shutdown.

Preserve upstream's separate high-priority, non-CoDel path for direct nested UDF
callbacks. Both ingress paths continue to share the dependency patch's physical
worker capacity and reserve. Buffer direct internal callbacks so a per-client-
ineligible request cannot hide eligible work for another client, and preserve
internal-callback dispatch priority over external expiry cleanup.

Discard callers that close while buffered or waiting for an active permit, and
rely on cancellation-safe permit handoff so abandoned work cannot leak active
capacity. Complete generic CoDel and lane-aware receiver shutdown, retained-
entry draining, deadline replacement and wakeup, and out-of-lock request/timer
destruction semantics.

Classify the five backend-owned analysis and configuration request variants
only when the deployment lane is enabled. Keep them inside shared-base queue and
worker capacity with no dependency reserve, action-shell accounting, priority,
or dedicated worker, and reject closed callers before assignment.

Expose strict self-hosted settings and bounded queue, scheduler, delay, expiry,
rejection, and enablement metrics. Initialize every valid queue rejection and
overload-transition label combination at zero and document the combined
rollout, rollback, cancellation, and telemetry contract.
